  1715	## Verification fixes (verify-1.1b-r1)
  1716	
  1717	Codex verified `9ee7fb8` (report
  1718	`/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3/ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/verify-1.1b-r1.md`):
  1719	APPROVE WITH EDITS, no blocking findings. Commit `6217868` fixes each edit.
  1720	Tests were written before the fixes; the Rust rollback tests (unresolved names)
  1721	and the repro manifest test were observed failing first:
  1722	
  1723	- **Sweep classification.** `classify` matched inputs only, so a trace corrupted
  1724	  at `public.day` on a D1 line was reported as D1 with `new_divergences: 0`.
  1725	  `confirmed_class` now requires the observed signature: D2 needs a `rejected`
  1726	  record, `TypeError: unhashable type` and Rust `rust_accepted`; D1 needs a
  1727	  Python-accepted transition and a Rust recheck, with only that line's Unicode
  1728	  digits spelled in ASCII, that passes the line. Receipt:
  1729	  `verify-r1/negative-classification.log` (the reviewer's corruption,
  1730	  `{'unclassified': 1}`, new 1).
  1731	- **Null probe.** `None` was the no-script sentinel, so probe 296 (`null` whole
  1732	  action) submitted PASS. `scripted_choices` submits scripted actions exactly;
  1733	  probe 296 now records `null`, Python accepts it and Rust agrees.
  1734	- **Rollback check.** Rejected steps compared order-insensitive `Value`s and
  1735	  skipped statuses/rewards/done. `rollback_difference` compares public and
  1736	  private values and key order, statuses, rewards and completion; three Rust
  1737	  tests cover key-order-only, private-order and scalar mutations.
